messages:
Anya P: Heads-up PR #4890 needs a fast pass. We updated the stream API and adjusted pagination fields last sprint. Can we update examples (py/ts/go) and add a tiny migration note?
Sam W: Ill take Go. I'll show an explicit before/after and a one-line pagination mapping.
Mike L: Picking Python. I want to show context-manager iteration + a compact retry decorator with a capped backoff. Keep it copy-paste friendly.
Nina K: I'll update TypeScript snippets and fix import paths. Will also search for any stale anchors.
Priya S: If anyone touches batching notes, ping me. We changed how streaming interacts with the batching thresholds and a short paragraph needs rewording.
Tariq M: I'll scan the console examples to ensure the Run sample still matches the snippets.
docs-bot: CI: build failed for PR #4890  linkcheck: /docs/streams_deprecated.md -> 404.
Anya P: Replace the dead link with /docs/streams and add this one-sentence migration blurb near the top: "Pagination params changed: page -> page_token, per_page -> page_size; responses now include next_page_token."
Sam W: Go snippet (old vs new):
```go
// old event-style
r, _ := client.Stream(ctx, req)
for chunk := range r.Chunks() {
  fmt.Println(chunk.Text)
}

// new iterator
it := client.StreamIter(ctx, req)
for it.Next() {
  fmt.Println(it.Value().Text)
}
```
Mike L: Python snippet + tiny retry helper:
```py
import time

def retry_simple(fn, tries=3):
    for i in range(tries):
        try:
            return fn()
        except TransientError:
            time.sleep(min(2 ** i, 4))
    raise

with client.stream_iter(prompt) as it:
    for chunk in it:
        print(chunk.text)
# tip: avoid retrying on 4xx client errors; keep retries short for UX
```
Nina K: TypeScript snippet (convert events -> async iterator):
```ts
// previous
const s = client.stream(req)
s.on('data', c => console.log(c.text))

// current
try {
  for await (const chunk of client.streamIter(req)) {
    console.log(chunk.text)
  }
} catch (e) {
  // distinguish transient vs client errors
}
```
Anya P: Nice. Small docs notes: (1) add one-line mapping for pagination parameters next to the examples; (2) in the retry tip, explicitly say "do not retry on 4xx"; (3) keep the migration paragraph <3 sentences.
Priya S: FYI I trimmed the batching paragraph to clarify that streaming-first requests may bypass certain batching heuristics; kept a short example pointer.
Tariq M: Verified console Run example matches the new iterator shape and updated the sample output snippet.
docs-bot: Deploy preview created: https://deploy-preview-4890--docs.redwood.ai (linkcheck passed after replacing the broken link).
Anya P: Thanks all  merging in ~30m if CI stays green. If any edgecases around batching+streaming surface, we'll do a follow-up small PR. :sparkles:
